cloro | Founding Engineer, Data Scientist, Founding Operations, Founding Marketer | REMOTE (EU timezones) | Full-time |  https:&#x2F;&#x2F;cloro.dev&#x2F;careers&#x2F; 

cloro is one API for search and AI answers. You send a query, we return Google, Google News, ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, Grok and Copilot results as structured fields: the answer, the sources it cited, and the position each result held. Teams use it to measure whether their brand shows up in AI answers, and to stop maintaining eight scrapers that break whenever a provider changes its markup overnight.

We are bootstrapped, remote across EU timezones, and small enough that every role below works directly with the founders.

Open roles:

* Founding Engineer | $80k-150k | backend and infra, heavy on large-scale collection.  https:&#x2F;&#x2F;cloro.dev&#x2F;careers&#x2F;founding-engineer&#x2F; 

* Data Scientist | $60k-100k | turn our AI-search corpus into published research and track the engines as they change.  https:&#x2F;&#x2F;cloro.dev&#x2F;careers&#x2F;data-scientist&#x2F; 

* Founding Operations | $50k-80k | finance, ops, marketing and product systems. An all-rounder role for someone who would rather build a system than run a task twice.  https:&#x2F;&#x2F;cloro.dev&#x2F;careers&#x2F;founding-operations&#x2F; 

* Founding Marketer | $40k-70k | own SEO, content, and visibility in AI search.  https:&#x2F;&#x2F;cloro.dev&#x2F;careers&#x2F;founding-marketer&#x2F; 

We work AI-native: Claude and Claude Code are in the loop daily across
engineering, ops and marketing. Being genuinely good with these tools is
part of the job rather than a bonus.

Enveritas (YC S18, non-profit) | Backend Software Engineer | Remote (Global) |  https:&#x2F;&#x2F;enveritas.org&#x2F;jobs&#x2F; 
Enveritas is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit working on sustainability issues facing smallholder coffee farmers. We collect field data in 30+ countries and build systems for analyzing risks in coffee, cocoa, and tea supply chains (including EUDR-related deforestation checks).

* Backend Software Engineer (Python, PostgreSQL&#x2F;PostGIS, Docker, AWS, Terraform) - $135-$155k - https:&#x2F;&#x2F;enveritas.org&#x2F;jobs&#x2F;backend-software-eng&#x2F;#10d7adef8us  (worldwide remote)

Supero | Cloud &#x2F; Platform Engineer | REMOTE (SF Bay Area, CA, US · Bengaluru, KA, India) | Full-time |  https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.supero.dev&#x2F;careers&#x2F;cloud-platform-engineer&#x2F; 

We generate full-stack apps and deploy them — a generated app becomes a live URL, on our infrastructure or in the customer's own AWS or GCP account. It's in production and it has more shell script in it than it should. You'd own it, and the mandate is to make it boring. Kubernetes, GCP and AWS deploy paths, CI&#x2F;CD, observability, cost, tenant boundary.

No on-call rotation today — it's the founders and whoever last touched it. Building a real one is part of the job, not something you inherit alone.

4+ years production infra, Kubernetes past the tutorial, AWS and&#x2F;or GCP at depth. The rest is on the page, including the open problems that don't flatter us. I'm a co-founder — ask me anything here.

You can apply at:  https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.supero.dev&#x2F;careers&#x2F;cloud-platform-engineer&#x2F; 

